arm64: dts: rockchip: rock-pi-e: fix gmac2io RX delay

With rx_delay = <0x11> the 1 Gbit port (gmac2io, RTL8211F over RGMII)
on a ROCK Pi E v1.21 drops 35-45% of large frames on receive: the MAC
counts thousands of mmc_rx_crc_error per few thousand frames and TCP
bulk transfers stall. Transmit is unaffected.

Sweeping rx_delay with tx_delay = <0x26> (Linux 6.18, 355 MB HTTP
downloads, 5000 1400-byte flood pings):

  0x08, 0x12        broken / ~5% loss
  0x11 (current)    ~40% loss, bulk stalls
  0x14, 0x22        marginal (CRC errors, 5-37 MB/s)
  0x16 .. 0x20      0 CRC errors in 500k frames, 110-117 MB/s
  0x24 and up       no link-level connectivity

Use the middle of the clean window. A soak at 0x1b passed 2.49M frames
with no CRC errors (3.5 GB received, 600 MB sent). The RTL8211F
internal delays (rgmii-rxid / rgmii-id) do not work on this board.

The same change is meant for Linux upstream; this copy fixes the DT
U-Boot passes to the OS on the EFI boot path.
Applies to U-Boot v2026.04 (88dc2788).

--- a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/rockchip/rk3328-rock-pi-e.dts
+++ b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/rockchip/rk3328-rock-pi-e.dts
@@ -154,7 +154,7 @@
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&rgmiim1_pins>;
 	tx_delay = <0x26>;
-	rx_delay = <0x11>;
+	rx_delay = <0x1b>;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	mdio {
